>Seeing as how well my wish question got answered,  here's another great
>debatable question:
>        1)  What is the best monster to polymorph into when you have both
>
>            a ring of polymorph and a ring of polymorph control?

    This is largely a matter of the particular situation you find
yourself in. Some monsters can wear full armor (f), some helmets and
boots only (h&b), others none at all (n). To my knowledge monsters
capable of wearing partial armor can also wield a weapon. Some monsters
can lay eggs giving you a tame pet when the eggs hatch. For these
monsters it may be worthwhile to polymorph briefly into them for the
sole purpose of laying eggs. Remember to remove cloaks and suits of
armor when polymorphing into a monster which cannot wear them
((n) and (h&b) below).

Possible spoilers follow:








    When you are polymorphing keep in mind that when the hit points of
the monster you are reach zero, you automatically return to human form.
Thus if you are a monster that can wear only partial or no armor be
perpared to run.

    If you're in the early game and don't have much special
armor it's probably best to try a monster with the best fighting
ability, my favorite choice for this is the jabberwock. In the later
game, as has been pointed out before on the net (forget who, sorry)
xorns are useful for dealing with the mazes of hell, Vlad's castle,
and the stronghold level. One can also retreat into the rock if
severely pressed. For facing magic using monsters such as golden nagas,
lichs, titans, and the wizard, your best bet is probably the vampire
lord since they can wear magic resistant armor. Vampire lords also
levitate which is valuable for avoiding traps. A summary follows:

 monster        abilities                          armor

jabberwock      very powerful                      (h&b)
balrog          no prayer allowed if not chaotic   (h&b)
xorn            move through walls                 (h&b)
vampire lord    drain level, levitate               (f)
master lich     touch of cold                       (f)
cockatrice      lay eggs                            (n)
guardian naga   spit venom, lay eggs                (n)
purple worm     lay eggs                            (n)
dragon          breath weapon, lay eggs, levitate   (n)

     One problem with polymorphing is that occasionally NetHack will
polymorph you into a new character "You feel like a new man/woman".
Your stats change with this polymorph. This is sometimes to your
advantage and other times not. Also don't forget than when polymorphed
into a new character your name will change. If you save the game you
must type nethack -uname to restart. Where name is the name of your
new character.


